{
  "id": "1043",
  "title": "Can I Eat Chinese Books?",
  "level": "elementary",
  "date": "2020-09-26",
  "synopsis": "Lili explains to Ben why she is eating walnuts.",
  "audioUrl": "https://static.duchinese.net/documents/1043/74e2ccc2149e3258c69068566d838644d8ebc28b.mp3?1595237294",
  "series": null,
  "fullText": {
    "simplified": "我可以吃中文书吗？\n\n本：丽丽，你在吃什么？\n丽丽：这是核桃。我最近有考试。天天看书太费脑子了，得吃核桃补补。\n本：为什么吃核桃能补脑子呢？\n丽丽：因为核桃的样子像大脑的样子！中国人觉得一个东西像什么，我们吃了就能补什么。核桃的样子像脑子，吃了就能补脑子！\n本：那我可以吃中文书吗？我需要补补中文。",
    "traditional": "我可以吃中文書嗎？\n\n本：麗麗，你在吃什麼？\n麗麗：這是核桃。我最近有考試。天天看書太費腦子了，得吃核桃補補。\n本：為什麼吃核桃能補腦子呢？\n麗麗：因為核桃的樣子像大腦的樣子！中國人覺得一個東西像什麼，我們吃了就能補什麼。核桃的樣子像腦子，吃了就能補腦子！\n本：那我可以吃中文書嗎？我需要補補中文。"
  },
  "sentences": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "simplified": "\n\n",
      "traditional": "\n\n",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Can I Eat Chinese Books?"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "simplified": "本：丽丽，你在吃什么？",
      "traditional": "本：麗麗，你在吃什麼？",
      "pinyin": "běn lì lì nǐ zài chī shén me",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "simplified": "\n",
      "traditional": "\n",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Ben: Lili, what are you eating?"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "simplified": "丽丽：这是核桃。我最近有考试。",
      "traditional": "麗麗：這是核桃。我最近有考試。",
      "pinyin": "lì lì zhè shì hé tao wǒ zuì jìn yǒu kǎo shì",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "simplified": "天天看书太费脑子了，得吃核桃补补。",
      "traditional": "天天看書太費腦子了，得吃核桃補補。",
      "pinyin": "tiān tiān kàn shū tài fèi nǎo zi le děi chī hé tao bǔ bǔ",
      "english": "Lili: These are walnuts. I have exams these days."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "simplified": "\n",
      "traditional": "\n",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Studying every day is too taxing on my brain, I have to eat walnuts to replenish it."
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "simplified": "本：为什么吃核桃能补脑子呢？",
      "traditional": "本：為什麼吃核桃能補腦子呢？",
      "pinyin": "běn wèi shén me chī hé tao néng bǔ nǎo zi ne",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "simplified": "\n",
      "traditional": "\n",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Ben: Why can eating walnuts replenish your brain?"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "simplified": "丽丽：因为核桃的样子像大脑的样子！",
      "traditional": "麗麗：因為核桃的樣子像大腦的樣子！",
      "pinyin": "lì lì yīn wèi hé tao de yàng zi xiàng dà nǎo de yàng zi",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "simplified": "中国人觉得一个东西像什么，我们吃了就能补什么。",
      "traditional": "中國人覺得一個東西像什麼，我們吃了就能補什麼。",
      "pinyin": "zhōng guó rén jué de yí ge dōng xi xiàng shén me wǒ men chī le jiù néng bǔ shén me",
      "english": "Lili: Because the shape of a walnut looks like the shape of a brain!"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "simplified": "核桃的样子像脑子，吃了就能补脑子！",
      "traditional": "核桃的樣子像腦子，吃了就能補腦子！",
      "pinyin": "hé tao de yàng zi xiàng nǎo zi chī le jiù néng bǔ nǎo zi",
      "english": "Chinese people think that if there is something that looks similar, we can use that thing to replenish it."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "simplified": "\n",
      "traditional": "\n",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "The shape of a walnut looks like the shape of a brain, so we can use walnuts to replenish the brain."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "simplified": "本：那我可以吃中文书吗？我需要补补中文。",
      "traditional": "本：那我可以吃中文書嗎？我需要補補中文。",
      "pinyin": "běn nà wǒ kě yǐ chī zhōng wén shū ma wǒ xū yào bǔ bǔ zhōng wén",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "simplified": "",
      "traditional": "",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Ben: Can I eat Chinese books then? I need to replenish my Chinese."
    }
  ],
